DESCRIPTION >
    Dashboard overview: top pageview page_urls for a caller-supplied
    UTC-padded window intersected with a timezone-local day range
    (Promise.all batch). Tenant-scoped; prunes via (site_id, timestamp).
    Faithful 1:1 port of api/routes/dashboard.js:98-112 (queryName
    'dash_top_pages'). Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6):
    properties.site_id -> site_id, event -> event_type,
    properties.page_url -> page_url (typed, String Nullable per §2.6). No
    JSON-bag fields. Checked against edge_domains.pipe (also a page_url
    group-by) — DIFFERENT: edge_domains has no event_type/date filter and a
    different LIMIT (100 vs 500); not a duplicate.
    The live query interpolates 4 date-boundary values (built from
    currentPadded.from/to + ' 00:00:00'/' 23:59:59', and localDateFrom/To +
    ' 00:00:00'/' 23:59:59') plus tz directly into the SQL string; per
    doctor_token_verify.pipe's precedent (no raw interpolation of non-tenant
    runtime values), these are ported as required template params carrying
    the full boundary string as the caller already builds it
    (current_from_ts, current_to_ts, tz, local_from_ts, local_to_ts) rather
    than string-interpolated or re-concatenated inside the pipe.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.
    DEPLOY FIX (tb --cloud deploy --check, ST_Staging v4.6.4, round 2): after
    the date/datetime param fix, --check surfaced the tz twin of the same
    issue — BAD_ARGUMENTS "Cannot load time zone '__no_value__'" from
    toTimeZone(timestamp, tz) when tz was declared String(tz, required=True)
    with no default. Fixed by giving tz a valid default:
    String(tz, 'UTC') — --check now has a loadable timezone to inject.
    Real callers passing a real tz behave identically (UTC is only used
    when the param is genuinely absent, same as --check's placeholder
    case). Only the tz param changed — no other param or SQL logic touched.
    Re-validated via tb --cloud sql with the gating site's real tz post-fix;
    parity held (see batch dispatch report).
    DEPLOY FIX (tb --cloud deploy --check, ST_Staging v4.6.4): date/datetime
    params were declared String(param, required=True) then wrapped in
    toDateTime(...) — that combination failed with CANNOT_PARSE_DATETIME
    under --check's '__no_value__' placeholder injection (a non-date string
    toDateTime() can't parse). Fixed by declaring the param itself as
    DateTime(...) (matching the already-shipped Phase 4 pipes' proven
    pattern) and dropping the now-redundant toDateTime(...) wrapper — no
    SQL/filter logic changed, only the param type. Re-validated via
    tb --cloud sql with real values post-fix; parity held (see batch
    dispatch report).

NODE dash_top_pages_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        page_url,
        count() AS count
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$pageview'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(current_from_ts, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp <= {{ DateTime(current_to_ts, required=True) }}
      AND toTimeZone(timestamp, {{ String(tz, 'UTC') }}) >= {{ DateTime(local_from_ts, required=True) }}
      AND toTimeZone(timestamp, {{ String(tz, 'UTC') }}) <= {{ DateTime(local_to_ts, required=True) }}
    GROUP BY page_url
    ORDER BY count DESC
    LIMIT 500

TYPE endpoint
